---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="BeaconGuard Technical Documentation"
  description="Technical documentation for BeaconGuard consequential-action authorization, governing policy authority, execution controls, deployment boundaries, and verifiable decision evidence."
>
  <section class="stack-section docs-index">
    <p class="section-label">TECHNICAL DOCUMENTATION</p>
    <h1>BeaconGuard Technical Documentation</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      BeaconGuard independently authorizes consequential AI actions before execution. It evaluates the specific action being attempted under customer-approved governing policy and preserves the decision evidence needed for later verification.
    </p>
    <p>
      The technical architecture is organized around <strong>Govern · Authorize · Verify</strong>. Start with the product boundary and system architecture, then go deeper only where needed.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-index-grid">
      <section class="content-card docs-index-card">
        <p class="section-label">START HERE</p>
        <h2>Orientation</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/platform"><strong>Product Overview</strong></a><br /><span>What BeaconGuard authorizes and where the boundary sits.</span></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/architecture"><strong>System Architecture</strong></a><br /><span>Govern · Authorize · Verify.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="content-card docs-index-card">
        <p class="section-label">AUTHORIZATION</p>
        <h2>Policy and runtime</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/policy-model"><strong>Policy Authority</strong></a><br /><span>How approved controls become production authority.</span></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/enforcement-runtime"><strong>Enforcement Runtime</strong></a><br /><span>Exact-action authorization and one-time execution authority.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="content-card docs-index-card">
        <p class="section-label">ASSURANCE</p>
        <h2>Evidence and verification</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/compliance-audit"><strong>Evidence and Verification</strong></a><br /><span>Decision evidence, integrity, and reconstruction.</span></li>
          <li><a href="/sample-decision-record"><strong>Sample Decision Record</strong></a><br /><span>Illustrative authorization evidence.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="content-card docs-index-card">
        <p class="section-label">DEPLOYMENT & RESPONSIBILITY</p>
        <h2>Integration boundaries</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/deployment-integration"><strong>Deployment and Integration</strong></a><br /><span>Where the boundary sits and how systems integrate.</span></li>
          <li><a href="/control-responsibility-matrix"><strong>Control Responsibility Matrix</strong></a><br /><span>Who owns identity, authorization, execution, and evidence responsibilities.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="content-card docs-index-card">
        <p class="section-label">SECURITY</p>
        <h2>Threat and trust analysis</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/docs/threat-model"><strong>Threat Model</strong></a><br /><span>Primary threats, responses, assumptions, and residual risk.</span></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/dfd-threat-flow"><strong>Data-Flow Trust Analysis</strong></a><br /><span>Trust boundaries and authority transitions.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .docs-index-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:1rem; margin-top:1.5rem; }
    .docs-index-card h2 { margin-top:.2rem; }
    .docs-index-card ul { margin:.75rem 0 0; padding-left:1.15rem; }
    .docs-index-card li { margin:.85rem 0; }
    .docs-index-card span { color:var(--text-muted); font-size:.93rem; }
    @media (max-width:800px){ .docs-index-grid{ grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
